# .git is deliberately NOT ignored: `go build` stamps vcs.revision/vcs.time into
# the binary only when it can see the repository, and /versionz reports them.
#
# For the same reason, nothing tracked by git may be ignored here. Excluding a
# tracked path makes git inside the build see it as deleted, which stamps
# vcs.modified=true and makes /versionz report every release as a dirty build.
# Only untracked paths belong below. Note that git inside the build cannot see
# your global gitignore, so a directory ignored on your machine still shows up
# as untracked there and must be listed here.
aidlc-docs
.aidlc-rule-details
.claude
